# Ollama Modelfile - attaches your fine-tuned LoRA adapter to the base model.
#
# Your training run (train_unsloth.py / checkpoint-30) produced a LoRA
# adapter, and it's been converted to a llama.cpp-format GGUF
# (qwen2.5-7b-finetuned-lora.gguf, ~40MB). That file only contains the
# *delta* weights from fine-tuning - it is NOT a standalone model and can't
# be loaded by itself (that's part of why it "wasn't connecting": there was
# no code path attaching it to anything). Ollama's ADAPTER instruction is
# exactly for this: it loads the base model, then applies the adapter on top.
#
# Usage (run from inside this models/ folder so the relative paths below
# resolve - the parent folder name has a space in it, which trips up some
# tools if you reference it directly):
#
#   cd /path/to/terabit-studio/models
#   ollama create terabit-finetuned -f Modelfile
#
# Then in zenith/.env, uncomment/set:
#   MODEL_NAME=terabit-finetuned
#
# and restart the backend. Check the backend's startup logs / call
# GET /api/health to confirm which model is actually being used.
#
# If you retrain and get a new checkpoint, re-run `ollama create` with the
# same name to overwrite it - no .env changes needed.

FROM qwen2.5-7b-q4_k_m.gguf
ADAPTER qwen2.5-7b-finetuned-lora.gguf
